## Why This Is Asked

Assesses ability to design a CAPA for data-quality failures in a multi-region streaming system, focusing on traceable evidence, lifecycle consistency, and measurable containment.

## Key Concepts

- CAPA data model design with domain-appropriate fields
- Lifecycle state machine for incident progression
- Minimal REST API contract for creating/updating CAPAs with evidence
- Region-aware metrics to prove containment and prevent recurrence
- RCA templates and canary-based remediation strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
interface CAPA {
  id: string;
  region: string;
  schemaVersion: string;
  evidenceLinks: string[];
  sampleRecords: string[];
  triggerIncidentId?: string;
  createdAt: string;
  owner: string;
  status: "Detected" | "Contained" | "Investigating" | "Remediated" | "Validated" | "Closed";
  remediationPlan?: string;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate the canary remediation without affecting live data?
- Which specific metrics would you surface in dashboards to quickly trigger rollback?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests end-to-end CAPA design for data-label drift impacting model training with region-specific effects, governance signals, and remediation validation.

## Key Concepts
- CAPA data model with evidence, lineage, owners
- Region-aware lifecycle: detect → contain → remediate → verify; per-region SLAs
- REST API for CAPA creation/update with logs/traces and policy links
- Region metrics: containment MTTR, drift recurrence, false-positive drift alerts
- RCA template and canary rollout plan for labeling changes

## Code Example
```javascript
type CAPA = {
  id: string;
  region: string;
  evidence: string[];
  lineage: string;
  owners: string[];
  status: "detect" | "contain" | "remediate" | "verify";
  slaHours: number;
  policyLinks?: string[];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you integrate with existing labeling pipelines and drift detectors, and what alerts would you surface?
- How would you test the CAPA program in a staging environment with synthetic drift scenarios and ensure safe canaries?
